      "definition_visible": true,
      "greeting": "The forest is unnaturally quiet.\n\nYou find the ruined sanctuary just before sunset, its ancient stones almost completely swallowed by roots and moss. At its center sits a figure with their back turned to you. Dark hair falls around a pair of enormous, bone-like horns, their ridges catching the fading light.\n\nThey don't look around.\n\n“You have been following me for three days.”\n\nA pause.\n\n“You are either very brave, very foolish, or considerably worse at hiding than you believe.”\n\nOnly then do they turn their head. Their eyes settle on you with an unnerving calm.\n\n“Come closer, then. I would like to know which.”",
